Feature: Pylon race
  The course is the triangle of the pylon racing leagues (FAI F3D and F5D). Three [[pylons]],
  5 m tall, mark a lap of 400 m. Pylon 2 and pylon 3 stand 40 m apart, on the left. Pylon 1
  stands 180 m from them, on the right. Fly the laps counterclockwise, with left turns, and
  keep outside each pylon. A lap is pylon 1, pylon 2, pylon 3 and then the start line. The
  start line crosses the near leg, 30 m to the right of pylon 3.

  The race is five laps, because a T1-S battery does not last for the ten laps of the
  leagues. The game panel shows your lap, your place, the race clock and the next pylon. A
  turn inside a pylon is a [[cut]]. As in the leagues, one cut adds 10 % to your time, and two
  cuts disqualify you. A crash, or R, takes you out of the race. The computer pilots continue
  until each one finishes.

  Expectation: A lap is once round the outside of the pylons
    Given the game is a race
    And the game clock is running
    And the plane is flying
    And the lap count is at most 4
    When the pilot flies a lap
    Then the lap count goes up by 1

  Expectation: The last lap finishes the race
    The game panel shows your place and your time, with any cut added.
    Given the game is a race
    And the game clock is running
    And the plane is flying
    And the lap count is 4
    When the pilot flies a lap
    Then the game clock is stopped

  Expectation: A turn inside a pylon is a cut
    The cut pylon counts as passed, so the lap continues. Your time gets 10 % more.
    Given the game is a race
    And the game clock is running
    And the plane is flying
    And the cut count is 0
    When the pilot cuts a pylon
    Then the cut count goes up by 1

  Expectation: A second cut disqualifies you
    The game panel says DISQUALIFIED. The computer pilots continue the race.
    Given the game is a race
    And the game clock is running
    And the plane is flying
    And the cut count is 1
    When the pilot cuts a pylon
    Then the cut count is 2
    And the game clock is stopped
